more dignified appearance."},"mp":"500","evade":"6","price":"3000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1050215","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI113415","name":{"zh":"金海金氏","en":"The Kim clan of Gimhae"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"也称伽倻金氏，出自弁韩部落。始祖金首露于建立伽倻（又称加耶、伽耶），是以金官伽倻为中心的城邦联盟。伽倻以铁器制造与贸易闻名，为半岛南部重要政权，与三国时期完全重叠。作为连接半岛与外部世界的铁器贸易中心，伽倻在半岛政治格局中扮演了重要角色。其王族“金海金氏”后世繁盛，有约六百万后裔，为韩国第一大宗族。","en":"Also known as the Gaya Kim clan, originating from the Byeonhan tribes. The founding ancestor King Suro established Gaya (also written as Gayan or Kaya), a confederacy of city-states centered on Geumgwan Gaya. Gaya was renowned for iron Crafting and trade, serving as a vital power in the southern Korean Peninsula whose existence coincided fully with the Three Kingdoms period. As an iron trade hub linking the peninsula with the outside world, Gaya played a crucial role in regional politics. Its royal lineage, the Gimhae Kim clan, flourished in later eras with roughly six million descendants, making it the largest clan in Korea."},"talent":{"military":"6","commerce":"5","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"许黄玉","height":"很矮","shape":"较瘦"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1068","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[35,40,62,58,72,65],"title":1,"rank":"1","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007102","armor":"WP1011502","helmet":"WP1012302"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"185","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1068","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[35,40,62,58,72,65],"title":1,"rank":"1","loyalty"